# MUST BE INCONSISTENT: Model and Algorithm are disjoint. 3.1.23 defines the
# model as a representation of a system, entity, phenomenon, process or data,
# 3.3.6 the algorithm as a procedure determining parameters. A representation
# is not a procedure, and the difference between them is what training makes.
@prefix iso:  <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#> .
@prefix inst: <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989/instances#> .
@prefix ex:   <https://w3id.org/aias/example/iso22989/neg#> .
@prefix owl:  <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .
<https://w3id.org/aias/example/iso22989/neg02> a owl:Ontology ;
    owl:imports <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989/instances/2.0.0> .
ex:Thing1 a iso:Model , iso:Algorithm .
